  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is redecorating his house, and is now trying to decide which chairs to buy.\n\nThe furniture store Chef is visiting has WWW wooden chairs and PPP plastic chairs available.\n\nChef believes that each wooden chair will increase the stylishness of his house by 222, while each plastic chair will increase the stylishness of his house by 111.\n\nChef wants to buy exactly KKK chairs in total.\n\nIt is guaranteed that K≤W+PK \\le W + PK≤W+P.\n\nFind the maximum possible stylishness Chef can attain by purchasing exactly KKK chairs from the store.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains three space-separated integers W,P,W, P,W,P, and KKK — the number of wooden chairs available, the number of plastic chairs available, and the total number of chairs Chef wants to buy.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the answer: the maximum possible stylishness Chef can attain by buying KKK chairs.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤90001 \\leq T \\leq 90001≤T≤9000",
      "1≤W,P≤201 \\le W, P \\le 201≤W,P≤20",
      "1≤K≤W+P1 \\le K \\le W+P1≤K≤W+P"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n4 5 6\n4 5 2\n6 3 9\n3 3 3",
        "output": "10\n4\n15\n6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: There are W=4W = 4W=4 wooden chairs and P=5P = 5P=5 plastic chairs available. Chef wants to buy K=6K = 6K=6 chairs in total.\nIt's optimal to buy 444 wooden chairs and 222 plastic chairs, for a total stylishness of 2⋅4+1⋅2=8+2=102\\cdot 4 + 1\\cdot 2 = 8 + 2 = 102⋅4+1⋅2=8+2=10.\nTest case 222: There are W=4W = 4W=4 wooden chairs and P=5P = 5P=5 plastic chairs available. Chef wants to buy K=2K = 2K=2 chairs in total.\nIt's optimal to buy 222 wooden chairs, for a total stylishness of 2⋅2=42\\cdot 2 = 42⋅2=4.\nTest case 333: There are W=6W = 6W=6 wooden chairs and P=3P = 3P=3 plastic chairs available. Chef wants to buy K=9K = 9K=9 chairs in total.\nThe only option is to buy all the chairs; for a total stylishness of 6⋅2+3⋅1=12+3=156\\cdot 2 + 3\\cdot 1 = 12 + 3 = 156⋅2+3⋅1=12+3=15."
      }
    ]
  },
